melody:
# Verse 1. The pickup is three eighth notes ("Oh Dan-ny").
Oh Dan-ny boy, the pipes, the pipes are call-ing
B3/ C4/ D4/ E4. D4/ E4/ A4/ G4/ E4/ D4/ ~C4/ A3 r/
from glen to glen, and down the moun-tain side.
C4/ E4/ F4/ G4. A4/ G4/ E4/ C4/ E4/ D4(2) r/
The sum-mer's gone, and all the flow'rs are dy-ing,
B3/ C4/ D4/ E4. D4/ E4/ A4/ G4/ E4/ D4/ ~C4/ A3 r/
'tis you, 'tis you must go and I must bide.
B3/ C4/ D4/ E4. F4/ E4/ D4/ C4/ D4/ C4(2) r/
But come ye back when sum-mer's in the mea-dow,
G4/ A4/ B4/ C5. B4/ B4/ A4/ G4/ A4/ G4/ ~E4/ C4 r/
or when the val-ley's hushed and white with snow,
G4/ A4/ B4/ C5. B4/ B4/ A4/ G4/ E4/ D4(2) r/
'tis I'll be here in sun-shine or in sha-dow,
G4/ G4/ G4/ E5. D5/ D5/ C5/ A4/ C5/ G4/ ~E4/ C4 r/
oh Dan-ny boy, oh Dan-ny boy, I love you so.
B3/ C4/ D4/ E4/ A4/ G4/ E4/ D4/ C4/ A3/ B3/ C4(4)
